WEBVTT

00:02.360 --> 00:05.230
<b>#16 For a Desired Future</b>

00:03.990 --> 00:07.740
You've resorted to rather
heavy-handed methods...

00:07.980 --> 00:09.510
Acting Chairman.

00:09.510 --> 00:14.620
Nothing ever seemed to go my way.

00:14.990 --> 00:19.250
I don't want to damage
such a valuable commodity.

00:19.660 --> 00:23.630
I've been hoping you'd
come along willingly.

00:24.010 --> 00:29.630
I've finally found what I want to do
at this school. Responsibilities, too.

00:29.630 --> 00:34.730
You're an exceptional success
even by White Room standards.

00:34.730 --> 00:40.390
Don't you find the competition
at this school beneath you?

00:40.390 --> 00:43.770
There are lots of exceptional
people here, too.

00:44.080 --> 00:47.400
Plenty for me to enjoy until graduation.

00:47.400 --> 00:50.780
If you insist. Then...

00:51.280 --> 00:55.530
I'll subdue you with my fists.

00:55.770 --> 00:58.280
I won't have you claiming it's unfair.

00:59.060 --> 01:04.540
You're the White Room's
masterpiece, after all.

01:05.360 --> 01:11.130
<i>The only path to the future
is one I take for myself.</i>

01:26.730 --> 01:31.610
Noon

01:26.730 --> 01:31.610
Expulsion

01:27.620 --> 01:30.350
<i>It's so simple, it's barely even a code.</i>

01:32.460 --> 01:37.010
<i>At noon today in Area I2,
Ayanokoji-kun will be expelled.</i>

01:38.110 --> 01:40.620
Caught you! Finally!

01:40.980 --> 01:42.900
What are you doing here?

01:42.900 --> 01:45.820
Your score! Show me your score!

01:45.820 --> 01:48.130
What in the world are you talking about?

01:48.130 --> 01:52.310
I told you before!
I'm going to beat you in this test!

01:52.310 --> 01:54.460
Now show me your score!

01:54.460 --> 01:56.390
I've got 131.

01:56.390 --> 01:59.340
We may both be second-years,
but you're still my competition.

01:59.670 --> 02:02.550
I can't risk showing you my information.

02:02.550 --> 02:05.400
Chickened out after hearing my score, huh?

02:05.400 --> 02:07.260
Bet you're losing, right?

02:07.620 --> 02:09.450
Sorry, but I'm in a hurry.

02:09.450 --> 02:10.400
You're running away?!

02:11.120 --> 02:12.400
All right, fine.

02:12.740 --> 02:16.830
If I show you, will you
please stop stalking me?

02:16.830 --> 02:18.770
Found you!

02:19.160 --> 02:22.040
Hey there, Horikita-senpai!

02:22.400 --> 02:23.290
Who's that?

02:23.290 --> 02:26.290
Amasawa Ichika-san from Class 1-A.

02:26.800 --> 02:28.980
You're in the way, you know.

02:28.980 --> 02:30.550
I have a prior appointment.

02:30.550 --> 02:32.400
An appointment?

02:32.400 --> 02:36.370
This all looks less than mutual to me.

02:36.370 --> 02:37.360
Excuse me?

02:37.360 --> 02:40.290
Was there something you
wanted, Amasawa-san?

02:40.630 --> 02:43.770
Where are you off to, Horikita-senpai?

02:44.000 --> 02:46.730
Your designated area is nowhere near here.

02:47.340 --> 02:48.520
It wouldn't be...

02:48.800 --> 02:51.030
I2, would it?

02:51.720 --> 02:53.900
You seem to know a great deal.

02:54.320 --> 02:58.440
<i>Even using GPS search, it shouldn't be
easy to intercept someone like this.</i>

02:58.440 --> 02:59.410
<i>Which means...</i>

02:59.840 --> 03:02.940
Would you shut up and butt out already?

03:02.940 --> 03:04.410
Ibuki-san.

03:04.410 --> 03:09.180
Horikita Suzune

03:05.020 --> 03:06.540
My score is 145.

03:06.540 --> 03:09.560
What? Seriously? This sucks...

03:09.560 --> 03:12.050
I suggest you return to the test.

03:12.540 --> 03:14.950
You still have a chance to overtake me.

03:14.950 --> 03:16.720
Okay, but still...

03:17.110 --> 03:20.100
Why aren't you going after
your designated area?

03:20.730 --> 03:24.390
There's something I have
to do at my destination.

03:24.830 --> 03:26.800
This is your chance, Ibuki-san.

03:26.800 --> 03:28.060
Yeah, I guess.

03:28.650 --> 03:31.300
Then I'll gladly use it
to turn things around!

03:33.370 --> 03:37.030
So, why are you going to I2?

03:37.030 --> 03:40.810
I suspect you know that very well.

03:40.810 --> 03:42.220
Whatever do you mean?

03:42.220 --> 03:43.410
Don't play dumb.

03:43.640 --> 03:46.470
You left this paper by my tent.

03:46.470 --> 03:47.980
Why did you do it?

03:50.720 --> 03:55.030
Sheesh. You just love your
little games, don't you?

03:55.030 --> 03:56.180
Games?

03:56.180 --> 04:00.160
What exactly are you getting me
and Ayanokoji-kun mixed up in?

04:00.160 --> 04:02.300
Couldn't say!

04:02.940 --> 04:07.570
Looks like I'm mixed up in it
the same way you are, Senpai.

04:08.220 --> 04:11.650
I don't have time to play
along with your riddles.

04:11.650 --> 04:15.120
You don't know the first
thing about Ayanokoji-senpai.

04:15.120 --> 04:18.570
Acting like you're on the
same side is just cringe.

04:18.570 --> 04:23.330
Are you saying you know
more about him than I do?

04:23.590 --> 04:25.080
Oh, I sure do!

04:25.300 --> 04:27.650
I know <i>all</i> about him.

04:27.650 --> 04:30.820
What makes him so cool and smart...

04:30.820 --> 04:33.660
and why he's stronger than everyone else.

04:34.380 --> 04:37.840
So? What do <i>you</i> know about him?

04:38.140 --> 04:39.230
<i>What do I know?</i>

04:39.720 --> 04:45.470
<i>He's... Ayanokoji-kun is the first
friend I ever made at this school.</i>

04:46.160 --> 04:49.050
<i>At first I thought he 
was a normal student,</i>

04:49.620 --> 04:52.430
<i>but he's proven far more
capable than I ever imagined.</i>

04:53.020 --> 04:55.190
<i>My brother acknowledged him.</i>

04:55.960 --> 05:03.120
<i>But he wanted to hide that side of
him to live a quiet school life...</i>

05:04.140 --> 05:08.960
You're right. I may not
know much about him at all.

05:09.830 --> 05:17.000
But I intend to spend the time between
now and graduation learning more.

05:17.510 --> 05:20.300
As a classmate. As a friend.

05:20.720 --> 05:22.800
I'll learn far more than you know now.

05:23.130 --> 05:28.310
You think a peon like you
can be useful to him?

05:28.310 --> 05:31.410
Perhaps I'm not capable
enough for that yet.

05:31.870 --> 05:37.070
But I intend to become someone who
can help him when he needs me.

05:38.530 --> 05:40.630
What a joke.

05:40.630 --> 05:46.450
Ayanokoji-senpai would
never come to <i>you</i> for help.

05:46.700 --> 05:48.660
At the moment, perhaps not.

05:48.660 --> 05:51.390
You think that'll change in the future?

05:51.390 --> 05:57.180
Thanks to you, I know
something's happening at I2.

05:57.180 --> 05:58.880
You think you'll get there?

05:58.880 --> 06:02.420
Yes. I certainly think I will.

06:03.190 --> 06:07.360
If you're that determined
to make it to him...

06:07.360 --> 06:09.710
I guess I'll have a little fun!

06:14.420 --> 06:16.940
That's a "one point to me!" kinda thing.

06:21.420 --> 06:24.330
Don't worry. I'll give you time.

06:24.330 --> 06:27.420
Take as long as you need.
Five or ten minutes, even!

06:27.420 --> 06:28.700
One more time.

06:36.430 --> 06:38.660
You thought I just did judo?

06:38.660 --> 06:41.300
Better start thinking bigger.

06:43.660 --> 06:46.080
Who in the world are you?

06:46.550 --> 06:50.360
Well, first off, I'm pretty disappointed.

06:50.360 --> 06:54.940
You're not nearly as good as I expected.

06:54.940 --> 06:59.690
That's why Ayanokoji-senpai never
talks to you about anything.

06:59.690 --> 07:01.440
You say you want to help him,

07:01.440 --> 07:05.470
but I bet you want to know
what he really thinks of you.

07:06.570 --> 07:09.200
Maybe I do.

07:09.490 --> 07:13.620
But I want to hear it directly from him!

07:15.620 --> 07:20.680
It would just annoy me to tell
you, so let's finish this instead.

07:22.420 --> 07:24.400
Bye-bye!

07:27.390 --> 07:30.390
Yow! What a punch.

07:30.390 --> 07:34.640
Nice catch there! Wasn't expecting that.

07:34.640 --> 07:36.390
What are you doing here?!

07:36.390 --> 07:38.750
I'm the one who's going to beat you.

07:38.750 --> 07:42.150
I won't let you lose to
some random first-year.

07:42.150 --> 07:44.940
I'm Amasawa Ichika-chan!

07:44.940 --> 07:49.320
Try to remember my name, 
okay, Ibuki-senpai?

07:50.870 --> 07:54.580
I'll keep her busy. You go on!

07:54.580 --> 07:56.250
What are you talking about?

07:56.250 --> 07:59.290
I thought you were trying
to beat me in the test!

07:59.290 --> 08:02.520
You're not going for your
designated area, right?

08:02.520 --> 08:05.760
There's no point in beating you like that!

08:05.760 --> 08:07.670
This is my fight!

08:07.670 --> 08:11.350
Yeah, right! I saw you
getting your ass kicked!

08:11.350 --> 08:13.600
You can't beat her!

08:13.600 --> 08:15.280
You don't know that!

08:15.280 --> 08:17.450
If you insist, I'll prove—

08:17.450 --> 08:20.560
Then prove to me how determined you are.

08:21.070 --> 08:23.440
Join my group.

08:24.410 --> 08:26.760
If one of us were to end up knocked out,

08:26.760 --> 08:29.360
we would immediately fail the
test due to dropping out.

08:29.360 --> 08:31.950
What a joke! Why should I work with you?

08:31.950 --> 08:34.950
If you can't commit
that far, then stay out.

08:36.740 --> 08:38.090
I don't like it.

08:38.090 --> 08:39.950
You don't have to.

08:40.460 --> 08:43.710
But if you're going to participate,
I want to know I can rely on you.

08:44.250 --> 08:46.290
I'd honestly rather be dead.

08:46.670 --> 08:50.480
But seeing you get expelled
by a first-year...

08:51.110 --> 08:52.480
would be even worse.

08:55.910 --> 08:58.240
Not a bad plan at all.

08:58.240 --> 08:59.510
You're both one-person groups,

08:59.510 --> 09:02.850
so dropping out means you're
expelled on the spot.

09:03.540 --> 09:06.200
But you've miscalculated on one thing.

09:06.200 --> 09:09.570
If it's okay for one of you to drop out,

09:09.570 --> 09:13.330
it's okay for me to break one of you.

09:13.330 --> 09:15.950
So, which will I crush first?

09:16.240 --> 09:17.780
Bring it on!

09:18.580 --> 09:19.230
Left!

09:19.230 --> 09:20.210
Don't give me orders!

09:31.590 --> 09:33.840
Okay, let's stop right there!

09:34.060 --> 09:36.350
This first-year is insane!

09:36.560 --> 09:37.920
Agreed.

09:38.470 --> 09:41.100
Okay, let's start again.

09:41.420 --> 09:43.600
<i>Why won't she just put us down?</i>

09:43.600 --> 09:45.610
<i>She's clearly good enough to do it.</i>

09:45.900 --> 09:46.830
<i>Can it be...</i>

09:47.610 --> 09:49.940
If she's looking down
on us, I'll teach her—

09:49.940 --> 09:52.660
If you want to work with me,
you have to do as you're told.

09:52.660 --> 09:55.020
What? Hell no!

09:55.020 --> 09:56.370
Ibuki-san,

09:56.370 --> 09:59.620
as a combatant, you're equal to me.

09:59.620 --> 10:02.300
No, perhaps a bit better.

10:02.300 --> 10:03.750
Where'd that come from?

10:03.750 --> 10:05.310
But that's all you have.

10:05.310 --> 10:08.420
You refuse to study.
You refuse to work with anyone.

10:08.420 --> 10:12.630
It's ridiculous for you to call
yourself my rival like that.

10:12.630 --> 10:13.770
Excuse me?!

10:13.770 --> 10:17.760
I think it's time for you to
break out of your shell...

10:18.230 --> 10:19.490
Ibuki Mio-san.

10:19.900 --> 10:21.270
What are you getting at?

10:21.270 --> 10:23.640
If you keep trying to bull
forward on your own,

10:23.640 --> 10:26.240
sooner or later, you'll get expelled.

10:26.240 --> 10:28.770
So what if I do?

10:28.770 --> 10:32.780
You'll have lost to me for good.
Are you all right with that?

10:33.650 --> 10:37.700
You can't be my rival if you're
expelled halfway through.

10:38.170 --> 10:43.040
Hang on until the end and
mature into a true threat.

10:44.090 --> 10:49.360
For that sake of that day,
just for now, lend me your strength.

10:49.920 --> 10:51.940
Fine, whatever.

10:51.940 --> 10:55.090
I'll shut up and do what
you want just this once.

10:55.090 --> 10:56.620
That's what you want, right?

10:56.620 --> 10:58.070
Perfect.

10:58.070 --> 11:01.400
So, what are my marching orders?

11:04.950 --> 11:07.620
Done with your planning time now?

11:22.540 --> 11:23.410
Now!

11:33.680 --> 11:36.510
You really got me with that one.

11:36.510 --> 11:38.090
It's over.

11:38.090 --> 11:41.380
You're lacking in stamina, aren't you?

11:42.270 --> 11:43.930
Secret's out, huh?

11:45.210 --> 11:47.520
How did you get that injury?

11:47.920 --> 11:53.280
I had a teeny little fight before
the one I had with you guys...

11:53.510 --> 11:56.220
You were fighting in that condition?!

11:56.220 --> 11:58.880
You wanna know who did it?

11:58.880 --> 12:00.990
Too bad I'm not telling.

12:01.240 --> 12:06.130
Things were just getting a little
interesting, but I guess it's time up.

12:06.130 --> 12:09.930
Go ahead and pass if you want!

12:10.310 --> 12:11.380
Though...

12:11.750 --> 12:16.380
I doubt there's any point in going
after Ayanokoji-senpai by now.

12:16.630 --> 12:17.710
Why?

12:17.710 --> 12:20.570
It'll all be over.

12:20.570 --> 12:22.010
What will happen to Ayanokoji-kun?

12:22.320 --> 12:24.890
Why not go see for yourself?

12:24.890 --> 12:27.730
I think you might regret it, though.

12:27.730 --> 12:29.680
What will you do?

12:29.680 --> 12:31.980
I'll go after Ayanokoji-kun.

12:32.280 --> 12:34.060
I'll go with you, then.

12:34.060 --> 12:37.740
If Ayanokoji's in trouble,
I wanna be there to laugh.

12:38.070 --> 12:39.980
What a spiteful attitude.

12:58.260 --> 13:01.380
<i>It's game over if I'm caught.</i>

13:01.660 --> 13:06.020
On paper, you should do everything
you can to avoid being surrounded...

13:06.020 --> 13:09.140
but is it really the wisest move here?

13:09.370 --> 13:14.020
You really aren't someone to trifle
with, Acting Chairman Tsukishiro.

13:14.020 --> 13:20.150
It's my job to do the work
nobody else wants to do.

13:20.150 --> 13:23.910
<i>I need to get this to one-on-one
before my stamina runs out,</i>

13:24.360 --> 13:25.660
<i>or this'll turn against me fast.</i>

13:27.150 --> 13:28.270
Acting Chairman.

13:30.520 --> 13:32.790
Isn't this a sight to see?

13:33.240 --> 13:37.160
What are you teachers doing to that
poor student all the way out here?

13:38.470 --> 13:41.760
I've been watching for a little while now,

13:41.760 --> 13:45.480
but I can't stand by and let
this two-on-one continue.

13:45.480 --> 13:49.470
I don't remember seeing you on GPS.

13:49.470 --> 13:52.560
Could this be the reason?

13:53.540 --> 13:55.110
Goodness me.

13:55.110 --> 13:58.570
So many technical issues with
the watches on this test.

13:58.570 --> 14:01.100
You're helping me?

14:01.100 --> 14:02.840
I don't know the situation,

14:02.840 --> 14:06.070
but it's the job of a third-year to
protect her underclassmen, isn't it?

14:06.070 --> 14:08.470
But what are you doing here?

14:08.470 --> 14:12.580
I saw you scrambling from the
first-years and got curious...

14:12.880 --> 14:17.090
and here I've found quite
an interesting situation.

14:17.090 --> 14:20.520
I don't know how helpful I can be,

14:20.520 --> 14:23.170
but it seems to me that you
won't last much longer.

14:23.170 --> 14:26.230
I'd appreciate every
second you can buy me.

14:26.230 --> 14:27.850
Listen to you.

14:28.070 --> 14:32.350
Shiba-sensei, I'll leave her to you.

14:32.350 --> 14:34.480
Still, Ayanokoji...

14:34.480 --> 14:37.250
Can't you put up a slightly better front?

14:37.250 --> 14:38.230
Uh...

14:38.470 --> 14:41.480
Show me the pose of a
man facing his destiny.

14:43.350 --> 14:45.440
Have you ever hit someone?

14:45.440 --> 14:49.220
I'm a lady. Of course I haven't.

14:49.220 --> 14:50.620
Seriously?

14:50.620 --> 14:56.630
Don't worry. I was just
itching to try it out.

14:57.550 --> 15:00.880
Let's finish this, Acting Chairman.

15:00.880 --> 15:05.760
You think you can beat me
if I'm by myself, then?

15:06.000 --> 15:09.520
Then why don't you show me...

15:09.520 --> 15:12.520
what you can really do?

15:51.740 --> 15:54.020
How long has it been since
I've experienced this?

15:54.490 --> 15:59.620
I acknowledge it.
You truly are a masterpiece.

16:01.040 --> 16:03.900
I don't like to get too rough,

16:04.560 --> 16:07.940
but I'm having so much fun,
I can't help myself.

16:17.160 --> 16:19.670
How did you know?

16:19.670 --> 16:21.920
Something felt off.

16:21.920 --> 16:25.170
Your glance at the ground, and how
you intentionally let your guard down.

16:28.090 --> 16:31.960
Well, what will you do now?

16:35.430 --> 16:39.940
I'm afraid you're out of
time, Acting Chairman.

16:41.040 --> 16:43.820
How did you get the boats here?

16:44.150 --> 16:46.780
You were laying groundwork in advance?

16:47.110 --> 16:53.070
I reported that there were students
from Class 2-A and 2-D collapsed here.

16:53.500 --> 16:58.080
The earlier incident confirmed that
the teachers would come to save them.

16:58.080 --> 17:01.580
So this was your intent from the start?

17:01.580 --> 17:05.340
Your lackluster attempt to
intimidate Ichinose failed.

17:05.600 --> 17:08.220
You should have been more
thorough in dealing with her.

17:08.220 --> 17:11.440
I'm still an educator, after all.

17:11.440 --> 17:14.590
I could never do something so violent.

17:15.100 --> 17:17.680
I'd like to know one last thing.

17:18.120 --> 17:22.020
Were you really trying to get me expelled?

17:22.020 --> 17:25.480
Surely there would be more
reliable ways to do it.

17:25.480 --> 17:27.980
You overestimate me.

17:28.380 --> 17:34.240
I was doing everything I could to
have you expelled. I simply failed.

17:34.660 --> 17:38.350
Could you take a message to Amasawa-san?

17:38.670 --> 17:39.850
Let's hear it.

17:40.560 --> 17:45.330
For failing to obey orders,
you're being declared a failure.

17:46.150 --> 17:50.680
You may remain at this school
or depart as you wish.

17:51.800 --> 17:55.820
Show me how you struggle to the very end.

17:57.230 --> 17:59.940
Well done, Ayanokoji.

17:59.940 --> 18:01.600
Same to you, Senpai.

18:01.600 --> 18:05.280
Don't worry.
I won't tell anyone about this.

18:05.660 --> 18:08.960
But it does make me want
to ask a few questions.

18:09.460 --> 18:12.610
I've just got a complicated
family situation.

18:12.610 --> 18:17.780
I see. Probably not something
I should pry into, then.

18:18.010 --> 18:19.620
Ayanokoji-kun!

18:46.120 --> 18:51.170
I hit an obstacle, but I hope you
haven't forgotten our agreement.

18:51.170 --> 18:52.520
Certainly not.

18:52.910 --> 18:55.690
Feel free to raise the
matter when the time comes.

18:59.850 --> 19:01.180
You had an agreement?

19:01.180 --> 19:08.420
I offered to grant Ryuen-kun one request
in exchange for his mercenary work.

19:08.420 --> 19:10.980
Was it all right for you to agree to that?

19:10.980 --> 19:17.220
Yes, I believe his request will tie the
noose around his own neck very soon.

19:17.890 --> 19:21.440
I'd like to repay my own debt to you.

19:21.440 --> 19:23.890
I only want one thing.

19:23.890 --> 19:29.270
To have an even match with you,
with no one to intervene.

19:29.510 --> 19:31.960
That may be difficult.

19:32.280 --> 19:34.550
There's no need to rush, of course.

19:34.550 --> 19:40.030
We still have nearly a year 
and a half left at this school.

19:43.040 --> 19:45.260
That sure was tough, huh?

19:45.260 --> 19:46.010
No kidding.

19:46.010 --> 19:47.790
I was seriously freaking
out for a while there!

19:48.120 --> 19:49.690
Just glad it's over.

19:49.690 --> 19:50.780
For real!

19:52.700 --> 19:53.910
What is it?

19:53.910 --> 19:56.300
N-Nothing.

19:59.540 --> 20:01.410
They'll announce the results soon.

20:06.070 --> 20:09.560
Well done completing the island test.

20:09.560 --> 20:16.690
It's time to announce the bottom
five groups who will be expelled.

20:16.910 --> 20:19.320
Class 3-D, Muto.

20:19.320 --> 20:21.850
Class 3-D, Kawakami.

20:21.850 --> 20:24.320
Class 3-C, Katsumata.

20:24.780 --> 20:27.210
Class 3-C, Shinonome.

20:27.460 --> 20:30.200
Class 3-B, Mikitani.

20:30.200 --> 20:32.700
As no measures were taken to save them,

20:32.700 --> 20:36.460
the fifteen members of these
groups will be expelled.

20:38.720 --> 20:42.210
<i>I would have expected
Nagumo to save them...</i>

20:42.210 --> 20:46.560
I will now announce the top three groups.

20:47.230 --> 20:49.980
In third, Class 2-A,

20:50.390 --> 20:52.430
the Sakayanagi Arisu group.

20:52.430 --> 20:54.300
261 points.

20:55.120 --> 20:58.110
In second, Class 3-A,

20:58.110 --> 21:00.200
the Nagumo Miyabi group.

21:00.200 --> 21:02.700
325 points.

21:03.640 --> 21:07.330
In first, Class 2-D,

21:07.860 --> 21:09.710
Koenji Rokusuke.

21:10.240 --> 21:12.670
327 points.

21:12.670 --> 21:15.810
We did it! We're Class C now!

21:15.810 --> 21:17.550
That's awesome!

21:17.550 --> 21:20.800
Koenji actually pulled it off!

21:20.800 --> 21:23.180
He really did see it through.

21:23.550 --> 21:25.810
This concludes my announcements.

21:25.810 --> 21:30.360
Please enjoy your dinner
and get some rest.

21:27.500 --> 21:30.860
It's hard to truly celebrate it.

21:30.860 --> 21:33.470
I think there's plenty to celebrate.

21:33.470 --> 21:37.190
We've escaped Class D for the second time.

21:37.190 --> 21:43.700
<b>Class A 1,206 Pt
Class B 578 Pt
Class C 571 Pt
Class D 551 Pt</b>

21:37.470 --> 21:41.430
True. We've taken a big step upwards.

21:41.430 --> 21:43.700
We're within spitting 
distance of Class B, too.

21:43.700 --> 21:46.950
That's a big increase in
our private points, as well.

21:46.950 --> 21:49.700
And it should improve class morale.

21:49.920 --> 21:52.460
Perhaps you're right.

21:52.810 --> 21:55.150
And it seems you made it through safely.

21:55.940 --> 21:59.460
Yes, perhaps I should just celebrate.

21:59.710 --> 22:01.080
That's for the best.

22:01.430 --> 22:04.080
I'm just fine, and completely unchanged.

22:05.020 --> 22:06.100
Completely.

23:40.540 --> 23:49.990
<b>Classroom of the Elite</b>

23:41.770 --> 23:49.990
<b>5th Season</b>

23:44.000 --> 23:49.990
<b>Confirmed</b>
